I've traced all the code paths. The issue is in `updateCommittedFullTranscript` in `v2_committed.go`. Let me show you.

`writeCommittedFullTranscript` (the initial write) correctly clears **all** entries at the session path before writing:

```go
// v2_committed.go:539-543
for key := range entries {
    if strings.HasPrefix(key, sessionPath) {
        delete(entries, key)
    }
}
```

But `updateCommittedFullTranscript` (used by finalization and migration repair) only clears v2-named files:

```go
// v2_committed.go:246-255
for key := range entries {
    switch {
    case key == rawTranscriptPath:           // raw_transcript
        delete(entries, key)
    case strings.HasPrefix(key, rawTranscriptPath+"."): // raw_transcript.001, etc
        delete(entries, key)
    case key == rawHashPath:                 // raw_transcript_hash.txt
        delete(entries, key)
    }
}
```

This doesn't clean up v1-named files (`full.jsonl`, `full.jsonl.001`, `content_hash.txt`). If an older version of the code wrote `full.jsonl` to `/full/current`, any subsequent `UpdateCommitted` call would write `raw_transcript` alongside the existing `full.jsonl` without removing it.

The fix is to also clear v1-named transcript artifacts in `updateCommittedFullTranscript`. Let me make the change.

